<title>UK: BT to win armed forces phone contract -report.</title>
<headline>BT to win armed forces phone contract -report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecom is expected to win a one billion stg contract to replace the vast private telephone network used by the British armed forces, the Independent newspaper reported.</p>
<p>The UK government will make the announcement in the House of Commons on Wednesday, the newspaper said. BT fought off Racal Electronics to win the contract, which is to renew the dedicated telephone and data network which connects UK military bases. The outdated network is run by BT.</p>
<p>BT on Sunday announced a $20 billion deal to merge with U.S. based MCI Communications Corp.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
